3 1 New Paragraphs; Food and Nutrition Programs. Amend RSA 189:11-a by inserting after
4 paragraphVIIIthefollowingnewparagraphs:
5 IX. Eachschoolboardmayvotetoraiseeligibilityforfreemealsto200percentofthefederal
6 poverty level. Meals served to students who meet the federal income eligibility guidelines shall
7 continue to be reimbursed in accordance with federal law and regulations. Meals not reimbursed in
8 accordancewithfederallawandregulationsshallbereimbursedbythestateofNewHampshireata
9 rate that covers 50 percent of the difference between the federal rate for a free meal and a reduced-
10 price meal, or the difference between a free meal and a paid meal. The remainder of the costs shall
11 becoveredbythelocaldistrict.
12 X.(a) The department of education shall adopt rules under RSA 541-A requiring school
13 districts that opt into the optional program pursuant to paragraph IX to offer both online and
14 physicalapplicationsforfreeschoolmeals.
15 (b) The department of education shall provide administrative or technical assistance to
16 school districts establishing an online application for free or reduced-price school meals, and whose
17 schoolmealprogramsareapprovedtooperatethroughtheUnitedStatesDepartmentofAgriculture.
18 (c) School districts eligible for administrative or technical assistance or funding under
19 this section shall be those approved to operate federal school meal programs through the United
20 States Department of Agriculture and accepted by the department of education to participate in this
21 expansionoffreeandreducedlunchbenefits.
22 2 Appropriation;DepartmentofEducation;FoodandNutritionProgram.
23 I. The amount of $107,000 is appropriated to the department of education for the biennium
24 ending June 30, 2026, for administrative costs related to providing administrative or technical
25 assistance to school districts establishing an online application for free or reduced-price school
26 meals. Thegovernorisauthorizedtodrawawarrantforsaidsumsoutofanymoneyinthetreasury
27 nototherwiseappropriated.
28 II. The amount of $250,000 is appropriated to the department of education for the biennium
29 ending June 30, 2026, for disbursement to school districts to be reimbursed at a 50 percent rate
30 pursuant to RSA 189:11-a, X(a) and to purchase software related to the establishment of an online
31 application for free or reduced-price school meals. The governor is authorized to draw a warrant for
32 saidsumsoutofanymoneyinthetreasurynototherwiseappropriated.
